---
title: Creme Brulee Custard
yields: 12%oz
serves: 4 3-oz portions
tags:
  - desserts
source:
  name: Serious Eats
  url: https://www.seriouseats.com/creme-brulee-for-one-from-paris-pastry-club
-- introduction: 
---

Prepare a #pressure cooker{} by placing a trivet and 1-2 cups of water in the bottom.

Set out 1/2-cup mason jars with coverings (either spent canning lids & rings or aluminum foil).

Add @heavy cream{250%ml}, @vanilla{1.5%tsp}, and @salt{0.25%tsp} to a small sauce pan and slowly bring to boil.

While its heating, whisk @egg yolks{5} with @powdered sugar{2.5%tbsp}.

When cream is at a low boil, slow whisk into egg mixture.

Once mixed, pour into mason jars (3 ounces each) and cover the jars.

Place on the trivet in the pressure cooker, cook for ~{6%minutes} and let naturally release.

Eat hot or chilled.
